# Cloudflare Pages security headers for the customer dashboard.
#
# Audit context: docs/internal/2026-05-20-csp-header-audit.md
# (TIER 5 security pass per FULL AUTOPILOT directive 2026-05-20).
#
# Prior state: NO security headers on the dashboard surface. Customer
# data (account info, API keys, billing, audit log) rendered without
# X-Frame-Options (clickjacking surface) or Content-Type-Options
# (MIME sniffing surface). This file closes the basic-header gap.
#
# Content-Security-Policy is DEFERRED to a follow-up — requires
# enumeration of inline scripts (Astro is:inline blocks on every
# page) + Sentry CDN domains + Stripe payment-portal redirect URLs.
# Adding CSP without that audit risks breaking the dashboard. Tracked
# in the audit doc above.
#
# Format reference:
#   https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# ── Hashed Astro bundles + CSS ───────────────────────────────────────
# Astro emits hashed filenames under /_astro/* — content-stable for
# the lifetime of a deploy.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Static media ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Self-hosted fonts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Geist (variable) + JetBrains Mono, vendored under public/fonts/ with
# their OFL.txt licenses. Filenames are unversioned but the binaries
# only change on an intentional font upgrade — treat as immutable.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Security headers — applies to every path ─────────────────────────
# X-Frame-Options DENY: prevents the dashboard from being embedded in
#   an iframe by any other site. Defeats clickjacking attacks that
#   would have a target site overlay invisible iframes over our
#   dashboard's revoke / pay / delete buttons.
# X-Content-Type-Options nosniff: blocks browsers from MIME-sniffing
#   the response body (especially relevant for the avatar presigned
#   URLs which could otherwise be re-interpreted as HTML).
# Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin: outbound clicks
#   from the dashboard (Stripe portal, docs, etc.) see only our
#   origin in the Referer header, not the full dashboard path the
#   customer was on.
# Permissions-Policy: deny camera/microphone/geolocation/USB/payment
#   etc. — the dashboard never needs any of these; explicit denial
#   eliminates an attack surface category entirely.
# Strict-Transport-Security: 2-year max-age + includeSubDomains + preload —
#   force HTTPS for the dashboard, which holds the ds_web_session_token in
#   localStorage. Without HSTS a network attacker could TLS-strip the first
#   visit and MITM the session token / credentials. Matches the API's HSTS
#   (apps/server/src/lib/app.ts). Added 2026-06-03 — the CF-Pages edge was
#   serving NO Strict-Transport-Security on this surface (verified live).
#   (The preload directive is advisory; hstspreload.org submission of the
#   apex is a separate founder/infra step.)
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
